   "_why": "DELIBERATELY STILL. This is a motion reference: the viewer compares one entrance against the last, so the only thing moving in frame must be the effect under examination. A travelling playhead lived here and was cut - it carried no information (progress through a 34s reel is not something anyone needs to track) and it pulled the eye sideways during every beat. The grid stays because a still workspace ground gives the white frame texture without competing."
  }
 ],
 "audio": {
  "silent": true,
  "_why": "a reference reel read frame by frame, not watched. A bed would set a pace the viewer is meant to ignore while they compare eight entrances against each other."
 },
