 "authoring": {
  "allow": [
   "numbered-section-markers",
   "static-bg"
  ],
  "_why": {
   "numbered-section-markers": "the numbers ARE the content: the reel is ordered by ascending After Effects labour, so 01..09 is the argument itself, not scaffolding above unrelated sections. This is the exemption the rule names.",
   "static-bg": "a motion REFERENCE, and the rule's own reasoning inverts here. The backdrop is normally the largest area of the frame and a frozen one reads as a slide - but this film's whole job is that you watch one entrance at a time and compare it to the last, so a second moving object anywhere in frame competes with the only thing worth watching. A travelling playhead lived here and was cut for exactly that. The film is not static: nine type effects animate in it."
  }
 }
}